---
title: Contribute
order: 1
description: Learn how islands can help improve the shared Knowledge Islands model through the Contribution Process.
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{% from "macros/icons.njk" import kiIcon %}

<section class="section-navy section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 56rem; text-align: center;">
    <p class="overline-gold">The shared model</p>
    <h1 class="heading-display-light" style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Contribute to the archipelago.</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.125rem; color: rgb(245 239 224 / 75%); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 52ch; margin-inline: auto;">Knowledge Islands grows through the experience of the islands that use it. A contribution is a proposal to improve the shared model in a way that can benefit more than one island.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-parchment section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div style="text-align: center; max-width: 52ch; margin-inline: auto; margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
      <p class="overline">Contribution Process</p>
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); margin-bottom: 1rem;">Improve what is shared.</h2>
      <p class="text-muted">The Contribution Process is the external path for proposing additions or changes to the common Knowledge Islands model. It complements, rather than replaces, the governance inside each island.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid-3col" style="gap: 1.5rem;">
      <article class="card-ki">
        <div class="symbol-circle symbol-circle-teal">{{ kiIcon("current", 22) }}</div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">1. Find a shared need</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">Start from a gap, pattern, or better approach that could strengthen the model for other islands, not only solve a local circumstance.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card-ki">
        <div class="symbol-circle">{{ kiIcon("compass", 22) }}</div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">2. Scope the proposal</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">A contribution needs clear boundaries and must be generic enough to belong in the canonical Library rather than one territory's local practice.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card-ki">
        <div class="symbol-circle symbol-circle-forest">{{ kiIcon("lighthouse", 22) }}</div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">3. Council assesses it</h3>
        <p class="text-muted">Arcadia's Council assesses proposals before a change enters the canonical record. Ratification is what keeps the shared model trustworthy.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-mist section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <div class="grid-2col" style="gap: 4rem; align-items: start;">
      <div>
        <p class="overline">Participation</p>
        <h2 style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Contribution is not internal setup.</h2>
        <p class="text-muted" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">Each island keeps its own Charter, Council, and local Contribution Process. Establishing those foundations is different from proposing a change to the shared model.</p>
        <p class="text-muted">If you are setting up an island, begin with the practical guidance. If you are refining the common model, use the Contribution Process as the governance boundary.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 2rem;">
        <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--color-teal); margin-bottom: 1rem;">A shared language</p>
        <dl style="display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; margin: 0;">
          <div>
            <dt class="heading-display" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Island</dt>
            <dd class="text-muted" style="margin: 0;">A discrete knowledge store with its own boundaries and internal governance.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="heading-display" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Territory</dt>
            <dd class="text-muted" style="margin: 0;">One or more islands under shared jurisdiction and governance.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt class="heading-display" style="font-size: 1.0625rem; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Archipelago</dt>
            <dd class="text-muted" style="margin: 0;">A natural grouping by proximity or shared character, distinct from governance.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-ocean section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 52rem; text-align: center;">
    <div style="color: var(--color-parchment); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">{{ kiIcon("archipelago", 32) }}</div>
    <h2 class="heading-display-light" style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Follow the model and the setup path.</h2>
    <p style="color: rgb(245 239 224 / 75%); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem;">The model explains the Contribution Process in context. Get Started explains how an individual island establishes the foundations to participate well.</p>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap;">
      <a href="/model/#processes" class="btn-primary">Study the Contribution Process</a>
      <a href="/docs/get-started/" class="btn-ghost-light">Establish an Island</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
